# An image is built from the source in this repository and nothing else. Without this file,
# `COPY . /src` in docker/release/Dockerfile copies whatever a working copy has accumulated,
# above all `results/`, which holds journals and can be gigabytes, into the build of an image
# that is reproducible from the source alone. Patterns are relative to the root of the
# context; `**/` matches at any depth.
results/
dist/
**/build/
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.toc
paper/*.fls
paper/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.synctex.gz
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Hidden files and directories at the root (the git directory, virtual environments, tool
# and editor state) stay out of the context, except the three configuration files the
# repository tracks.
.*
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.dockerignore
